## 1. Scope

This audit covers human authentication, RBAC, API keys, agent credentials, token/session behavior, environment scoping, frontend permission drift, and SDK authentication ergonomics. It inspects `product_platform/api/auth.py`, `api/rbac.py`, API-key models/routes/repositories, Tool Gateway auth, frontend RBAC, and SDK token providers. Relevant benchmarks are Microsoft enterprise access controls, AWS AgentCore Identity, Google IAM integration, Arcade/Composio user-specific authorization, and OpenAI approval patterns. Out of scope: provider credential storage, which is covered in INT.

## 2. Current Implementation Summary

The backend has local token issuance and validation in `packages/product-platform/src/product_platform/api/auth.py`, RBAC constants in `api/rbac.py`, tenancy/environment middleware in `api/app.py`, API key tables in `0001_base_schema.up.sql`, and environment scope migration `0064_api_key_environment_scope.up.sql`. API key hashing uses PBKDF2 plus pepper in `api/api_keys.py:169`. Tool Gateway principal resolution uses agent credentials in `tool_gateway/auth.py` and supports bearer-token based SDK calls. The Python SDK has static and environment token providers in `ophanix-python-sdk/src/ophanix_tool_gateway/sdk.py`.

Current workflow: users authenticate with local HMAC-style tokens, roles are enforced through backend permission constants, API keys can be created/revoked, agent credentials can authenticate gateway calls, and frontend route guards use a separate permission map. Enterprise IdP fields exist in settings but there is no observed OIDC/JWKS/SAML validation path.

